1
00:00:00,742 --> 00:00:06,746
[A Bona Fide Killer]

2
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:09,760
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:10,760
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,760
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

5
00:00:16,083 --> 00:00:21,221
[Winter, 2011]

6
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:26,432
Come on, I told you to order something
expensive. Get some boiled pork too.

7
00:00:26,432 --> 00:00:28,016
You're a college student.
How much money could you have?

8
00:00:28,016 --> 00:00:30,004
It's fine. This is enough.

9
00:00:30,004 --> 00:00:32,276
I work part-time.

10
00:00:32,276 --> 00:00:33,844
I have more money than you.

11
00:00:33,844 --> 00:00:36,052
How? You're just
a civil service exam student.

12
00:00:36,052 --> 00:00:37,775
My mom.

13
00:00:38,528 --> 00:00:40,875
She's been saving up more than I realized.

14
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:46,168
Is studying for the police exam going okay?

15
00:00:46,168 --> 00:00:47,532
I guess it's just right for me.

16
00:00:47,532 --> 00:00:48,904
It really sticks in my head.

17
00:00:48,904 --> 00:00:50,328
Just wait and see.

18
00:00:50,328 --> 00:00:55,160
I'll be wearing a badge within two years,
and I'll catch that punk myself.

19
00:00:55,160 --> 00:00:57,152
And then what, after you catch him?

20
00:00:57,152 --> 00:00:58,700
After that?

21
00:00:58,700 --> 00:00:59,968
Then I'll catch the next punk.

22
00:00:59,968 --> 00:01:01,708
Jeez, forget it, you punk.

23
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:05,341
You talked me into being a reporter,
and now you're betraying me.

24
00:01:05,341 --> 00:01:06,741
The more I think about it,
the more pissed off I get.

25
00:01:06,741 --> 00:01:10,276
Hey, if we're all digging,
who's going to catch the fish?

26
00:01:10,276 --> 00:01:11,960
You just keep digging.

27
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:13,716
I'll catch the fish.

28
00:01:13,716 --> 00:01:16,196
You do your job, and I'll do mine.

29
00:01:16,196 --> 00:01:17,728
Bang, bang!

30
00:01:17,728 --> 00:01:18,836
Oh, please.

31
00:01:18,836 --> 00:01:21,296
Don't get beaten to a pulp
by some criminal later.

32
00:01:21,296 --> 00:01:24,280
- Ma'am, could you turn up the TV?
- Sure.

33
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:26,761
[Police Focused on Kingfisher Investigation]
<i>The shooting incidents</i>

34
00:01:26,761 --> 00:01:30,692
<i>by the serial killer known as Kingfisher
have risen to nine.</i>

35
00:01:30,692 --> 00:01:34,112
<i>Police have concluded that
last week's shooting in Cheongsin-dong</i>

36
00:01:34,112 --> 00:01:36,148
[Kingfisher Shootings Rise to 9]
<i>was also the work of the same suspect.</i>

37
00:01:36,148 --> 00:01:38,975
[Cheongsin-dong Case Also Same Culprit]
<i>They are intensifying their investigation.</i>

38
00:01:38,975 --> 00:01:43,000
<i>Meanwhile, the number of members
in an online Kingfisher fan club</i>

39
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,628
- <i>is approaching 300,000...</i>
- A fan club?

40
00:01:44,628 --> 00:01:46,275
Have they all lost their darn minds?

41
00:01:46,275 --> 00:01:48,175
Why are they cheering for that lunatic?

42
00:01:48,175 --> 00:01:50,612
Maybe they get
some kind of catharsis from it.

43
00:01:50,612 --> 00:01:53,241
He picks out the worst criminals
and kills them.

44
00:01:53,241 --> 00:01:54,308
Catharsis, my foot.

45
00:01:54,308 --> 00:01:58,664
Hey, isn't killing a murderer still murder?

46
00:01:58,664 --> 00:02:00,912
Even if he only kills criminals for now,

47
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:03,375
who's to say he won't kill
an innocent person someday?

48
00:02:04,269 --> 00:02:08,241
If, by chance, I mean, seriously, what if...

49
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,840
just hypothetically,
Kingfisher killed that punk...

50
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:14,775
That punk? Who...

51
00:02:17,141 --> 00:02:20,424
Do you really think
I'd feel happy or thankful?

52
00:02:20,424 --> 00:02:23,108
I mean, he'd be taking revenge
for you, or something like that.

53
00:02:23,108 --> 00:02:25,168
Darn it. Hey!

54
00:02:25,168 --> 00:02:28,836
If another murderer kills
my parents' murderer, is that revenge?

55
00:02:28,836 --> 00:02:30,640
If anyone's going to take revenge,
it should be me.

56
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,808
What right does Kingfisher have?

57
00:02:38,688 --> 00:02:40,975
My revenge is

58
00:02:40,975 --> 00:02:44,708
to catch him and put him
in prison for the rest of his life.

59
00:02:44,708 --> 00:02:47,668
To me, they're both the same murdering punk.

60
00:02:47,668 --> 00:02:50,200
Once I catch that punk,

61
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:54,541
I'll catch Kingfisher next, no matter what.

62
00:02:55,444 --> 00:02:57,692
Just wait and see.

63
00:02:57,692 --> 00:02:59,392
Alright.

64
00:03:03,741 --> 00:03:04,868
Oh, my.

65
00:03:04,868 --> 00:03:07,764
Oh, my, I'm so sorry.

66
00:03:07,764 --> 00:03:10,948
Ma'am, one plate of boiled pork, please.

67
00:03:10,948 --> 00:03:12,368
To cover the dry cleaning.

68
00:03:12,368 --> 00:03:15,075
Keep your strength up, future detective.

69
00:03:16,692 --> 00:03:19,208
Thirty thousand won,
including the boiled pork? Alright.

70
00:03:19,208 --> 00:03:20,908
What's with her?

71
00:03:28,218 --> 00:03:30,643
[Episode 10]

72
00:03:31,017 --> 00:03:32,784
[Client Suitability Assessment,
One-Month Post-Release Observation]

73
00:03:32,808 --> 00:03:34,385
[Multiple Risk Indicators,
High Reoffending Risk]

74
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:46,141
Why? Because of the victim's son who's a cop?

75
00:03:50,896 --> 00:03:54,568
I thought he looked familiar. Now I remember.

76
00:03:54,568 --> 00:03:59,768
I saw him in the first-floor lobby
when we were leaving your housewarming party.

77
00:03:59,768 --> 00:04:01,944
I've heard about it.

78
00:04:01,944 --> 00:04:03,720
He's a friend of my husband's.

79
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,004
Yeah?

80
00:04:05,004 --> 00:04:06,704
Your husband...

81
00:04:07,728 --> 00:04:10,075
had a friend like that?

82
00:04:10,768 --> 00:04:15,875
If you're really uncomfortable with it,
let's change the scenario.

83
00:04:22,075 --> 00:04:24,924
Why do people never really change?

84
00:04:24,924 --> 00:04:27,592
Twenty years is a pretty long time.

85
00:04:27,592 --> 00:04:29,292
Exactly.

86
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:32,408
They commit sins
that even repentance and remorse

87
00:04:32,408 --> 00:04:35,388
can never make the victims' families forgive.

88
00:04:35,388 --> 00:04:37,040
Why do they even do it?

89
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,775
At times like this,

90
00:04:39,408 --> 00:04:44,908
that saying, "A leopard can't change
its spots," feels so cruel, doesn't it?

91
00:04:44,908 --> 00:04:49,144
But still, not everyone kills just because

92
00:04:49,144 --> 00:04:51,475
they grew up in different
conditions and environments.

93
00:04:51,475 --> 00:04:57,951
Plenty of people serve the time they deserve
and then go on to live new lives.

94
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:02,875
That's why the law and the state
give them another chance.

95
00:05:06,492 --> 00:05:08,675
Let's stick to the scenario.

96
00:05:09,372 --> 00:05:11,075
Will you be okay?

97
00:05:11,758 --> 00:05:12,758
I have to be.

98
00:05:12,758 --> 00:05:16,941
It's my job, and it's what I can do.

99
00:05:29,884 --> 00:05:31,575
<i>Why are you going after that punk, you idiot?</i>

100
00:05:31,575 --> 00:05:34,508
What are you planning to do if you meet him?

101
00:05:35,256 --> 00:05:38,224
What do you mean? I'm just watching him.

102
00:05:38,224 --> 00:05:39,872
Why? What...

103
00:05:39,872 --> 00:05:41,908
Worried the cop might do something reckless?

104
00:05:41,908 --> 00:05:43,560
Especially since I have a gun?

105
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:46,488
Jeez, even your jokes are messed up.

106
00:05:46,488 --> 00:05:48,780
- Why do you have a gun...
- <i>If you know I'm joking,</i>

107
00:05:48,780 --> 00:05:51,420
stop worrying and go home.

108
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,200
Didn't you say
your wife's working late tonight?

109
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,900
<i>I'm hanging up.</i>

110
00:06:16,513 --> 00:06:17,448
[My Santa]

111
00:06:17,472 --> 00:06:19,136
<i>I'm working late.</i>

112
00:06:19,136 --> 00:06:20,668
<i>Where are you, Tae Seong?</i>

113
00:06:20,668 --> 00:06:22,141
<i>I'm leaving work now.</i>

114
00:06:22,141 --> 00:06:25,804
<i>Se Ah said she'd watch Yul until eight.
I'll make sure I get home before then.</i>

115
00:06:25,804 --> 00:06:27,972
<i>I won't be too late either.</i>

116
00:06:27,972 --> 00:06:29,175
<i>I'll call you when I'm done.</i>

117
00:06:29,408 --> 00:06:30,926
[Wednesday, May 6]

118
00:06:31,932 --> 00:06:34,440
<i>Jang Eun Hak is leaving work.</i>

119
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,824
He's expected to arrive in
about five minutes.

120
00:06:36,824 --> 00:06:38,524
<i>Okay.</i>

121
00:06:44,541 --> 00:06:46,808
He's entering the next block.

122
00:06:56,860 --> 00:07:00,375
Looks like he's buying something.
He just went into a convenience store.

123
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:03,208
<i>Oh...</i>

124
00:07:03,208 --> 00:07:05,092
It's liquor.

125
00:07:05,092 --> 00:07:09,548
He grabbed a few bottles of soju
and sat down outside the store.

126
00:07:09,548 --> 00:07:11,475
<i>This could take a while.</i>

127
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:24,876
Ms. Yoo, there's a man tailing Jang Eun Hak.

128
00:07:24,876 --> 00:07:26,567
- A man?
- <i>Looks like he's been following him</i>

129
00:07:26,567 --> 00:07:27,689
<i>since the workshop.</i>

130
00:07:27,689 --> 00:07:30,360
He's watching him from a distance.

131
00:07:30,360 --> 00:07:31,900
What does he look like?

132
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,888
Wearing a jacket, mid-thirties, maybe?

133
00:07:34,888 --> 00:07:38,420
I can't make out his face on camera.

134
00:07:38,420 --> 00:07:40,141
Let me take a look.

135
00:08:03,124 --> 00:08:06,020
Could it be the son who's a cop...

136
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:07,628
Yeah, that's him.

137
00:08:07,628 --> 00:08:09,441
Then I guess today...

138
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,608
Let's just watch for now.

139
00:08:26,408 --> 00:08:28,308
Jang Eun Hak is moving.

140
00:08:29,228 --> 00:08:31,884
He's heading back the way he came?

141
00:08:31,884 --> 00:08:33,584
I see him.

142
00:08:51,444 --> 00:08:53,841
Jang Eun Hak has gone back into the workshop.

143
00:09:01,648 --> 00:09:05,044
Ms. Yoo, Jang Eun Hak made a move again.

144
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:07,575
What? What about the son?

145
00:09:08,736 --> 00:09:10,436
What? Is he hurt?

146
00:09:12,368 --> 00:09:14,704
<i>Jang Eun Hak bolted out.</i>

147
00:09:14,704 --> 00:09:17,308
<i>The son chased right after him.</i>

148
00:09:17,308 --> 00:09:19,441
[Dongwoon Furniture]
He's holding a gun.

149
00:09:37,148 --> 00:09:38,224
I'm heading out.

150
00:09:38,224 --> 00:09:40,108
<i>Track their route and keep me posted.</i>

151
00:09:40,108 --> 00:09:44,068
Ms. Yoo, Kwon Tae Seong is here.

152
00:09:44,068 --> 00:09:45,472
- What?
- <i>He went into the workshop,</i>

153
00:09:45,472 --> 00:09:49,175
came back out, and ran off
in the direction the two of them went.

154
00:09:49,175 --> 00:09:51,060
Why is your husband here...

155
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:53,844
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo, are you listening?

156
00:09:53,844 --> 00:09:55,236
Yeah, I'm listening.

157
00:09:55,236 --> 00:09:57,184
- Then let's pull out for today...
- No.

158
00:09:57,184 --> 00:09:58,544
<i>If we leave now, we'll lose him.</i>

159
00:09:58,544 --> 00:10:00,244
Keep going.

160
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,080
I'm down. Which way?

161
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,875
<i>Ms. Yoo, what are you going to do?</i>

162
00:10:06,875 --> 00:10:08,268
What if something happens today...

163
00:10:08,268 --> 00:10:09,968
<i>Ki Yeong Do.</i>

164
00:10:14,575 --> 00:10:16,375
With your back to the workshop,
you are on the left.

165
00:10:16,375 --> 00:10:19,348
<i>It's to your right, Ms. Yoo.</i>

166
00:10:19,348 --> 00:10:21,675
Don't take any unnecessary risks.

167
00:11:13,716 --> 00:11:15,741
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

168
00:11:35,568 --> 00:11:37,408
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

169
00:11:54,580 --> 00:11:56,280
Meeting concluded.

170
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,368
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

171
00:12:00,368 --> 00:12:03,052
You should get out of there for now.

172
00:12:03,052 --> 00:12:04,752
Dong Jin!

173
00:12:14,284 --> 00:12:15,341
What's wrong with you?

174
00:12:15,341 --> 00:12:17,041
Are you okay?

175
00:12:18,244 --> 00:12:19,944
No...

176
00:12:20,664 --> 00:12:22,744
Not me. I didn't shoot him.

177
00:12:22,744 --> 00:12:26,844
- I know, I know.
- Not me... I...

178
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,780
Kingfisher...

179
00:12:35,284 --> 00:12:37,192
Kingfisher was here.

180
00:12:37,192 --> 00:12:38,756
Kingfisher was here... Kingfisher...

181
00:12:38,756 --> 00:12:40,684
Kingfisher... Kingfisher...

182
00:12:40,684 --> 00:12:42,668
Kingfisher...

183
00:12:42,668 --> 00:12:45,375
Dong Jin!

184
00:12:46,141 --> 00:12:47,141
Dong Jin!

185
00:12:47,141 --> 00:12:48,875
No.

186
00:12:49,508 --> 00:12:50,875
You need to get to a hospital first.

187
00:12:50,875 --> 00:12:52,575
You're hurt right now.

188
00:12:52,575 --> 00:12:54,308
I have to catch him.
I have to catch Kingfisher.

189
00:12:54,308 --> 00:12:57,016
You're bleeding badly now!

190
00:12:57,016 --> 00:12:58,224
He was here.

191
00:12:58,224 --> 00:13:00,741
Kingfisher was right here moments ago.

192
00:13:00,741 --> 00:13:03,541
Lee Dong Jin, Lee Dong Jin.

193
00:13:04,164 --> 00:13:05,492
Pull yourself together.

194
00:13:05,492 --> 00:13:07,241
You have to stay conscious.

195
00:13:09,376 --> 00:13:11,076
Tae Seong.

196
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:16,341
That punk, Jang Eun Hak...

197
00:13:19,496 --> 00:13:21,196
is dead.

198
00:13:22,232 --> 00:13:24,008
That punk...

199
00:13:27,852 --> 00:13:29,508
He is dead, that punk...

200
00:13:29,508 --> 00:13:33,675
Tae Seong, what do I do? I'm...

201
00:13:36,336 --> 00:13:38,675
I'm so glad that...

202
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,775
Jang Eun Hak is dead.

203
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:46,180
And...

204
00:13:47,776 --> 00:13:50,144
I'm ashamed of myself for feeling that way.

205
00:13:50,144 --> 00:13:51,496
Dong Jin, it's alright.

206
00:13:51,496 --> 00:13:54,741
Dong Jin, it's alright. It's alright.

207
00:13:58,092 --> 00:14:01,808
I was the person in the world
who wanted Jang Eun Hak dead the most.

208
00:14:03,088 --> 00:14:08,732
Every single day, without fail,
I wanted to kill him.

209
00:14:08,732 --> 00:14:12,175
Even after twenty years,
whenever I think about that day...

210
00:14:21,076 --> 00:14:24,541
I imagined shooting him over and over again.

211
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:29,641
I imagined a hole blown through his head,
his entire body torn to shreds,

212
00:14:31,112 --> 00:14:35,167
writhing in agony, then falling into hell.

213
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:37,742
I wanted desperately to see it
with my own eyes.

214
00:14:37,742 --> 00:14:39,632
I know. I know, Dong Jin.

215
00:14:39,632 --> 00:14:42,724
But first, let's go to the hospital. Please.

216
00:14:42,724 --> 00:14:44,775
Dong Jin, Dong Jin.

217
00:14:44,775 --> 00:14:46,748
You need to go to the hospital first.

218
00:14:46,748 --> 00:14:48,775
I have to catch Kingfisher.

219
00:14:49,772 --> 00:14:52,244
He killed that punk!

220
00:14:52,244 --> 00:14:54,641
Kingfisher killed that punk.

221
00:14:54,641 --> 00:14:57,173
For twenty years you pictured it
over and over, but couldn't do it.

222
00:14:57,173 --> 00:14:59,208
Kingfisher did.

223
00:14:59,208 --> 00:15:00,675
You saw it, right?

224
00:15:00,675 --> 00:15:04,348
That punk was trying to kill someone again.

225
00:15:04,348 --> 00:15:07,148
That's right. I couldn't do it.

226
00:15:07,148 --> 00:15:09,640
Even when Jang Eun Hak
was running right in front of me,

227
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:12,975
with the back of his head
right there in front of me,

228
00:15:13,941 --> 00:15:15,708
I still couldn't kill him.

229
00:15:15,708 --> 00:15:17,441
Do you know why?

230
00:15:19,684 --> 00:15:20,756
You asked me before.

231
00:15:20,756 --> 00:15:23,168
What if he didn't change?

232
00:15:23,168 --> 00:15:25,296
But I already had my answer.

233
00:15:25,296 --> 00:15:28,224
If he commits a crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in.

234
00:15:28,224 --> 00:15:30,588
If he gets out and commits another crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in again.

235
00:15:30,588 --> 00:15:32,008
I'll keep catching him and locking him up.

236
00:15:32,008 --> 00:15:34,624
That's my way,
and it's the right thing to do.

237
00:15:34,624 --> 00:15:39,156
No, in reality, those punks never get judged.

238
00:15:39,156 --> 00:15:43,641
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

239
00:15:43,641 --> 00:15:45,141
Oh, yeah?

240
00:15:45,141 --> 00:15:47,341
Then do whatever you want.

241
00:15:47,341 --> 00:15:49,880
I don't care whether the law
is perfect or not.

242
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,220
To me, they're just the same punks
who killed people.

243
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:54,608
And catching punks like that is my job.

244
00:15:56,672 --> 00:15:59,688
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

245
00:15:59,688 --> 00:16:02,308
Write a story, cover a case, whatever.

246
00:16:02,308 --> 00:16:04,141
You're a reporter, right?

247
00:16:11,672 --> 00:16:14,075
Beom, where are you?

248
00:16:26,176 --> 00:16:27,368
Beom.

249
00:16:27,368 --> 00:16:30,312
Comb through all the nearby CCTV footage
and track his escape route.

250
00:16:30,312 --> 00:16:34,108
And collect every fingerprint, footprint,
and trace evidence around the rooftop.

251
00:16:34,108 --> 00:16:35,908
Okay.

252
00:16:50,716 --> 00:16:52,352
Se Ah.

253
00:16:52,352 --> 00:16:54,380
- Huh? Oh.
- Sorry for waking you.

254
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:55,744
Bo Na, you're home?

255
00:16:55,744 --> 00:16:59,160
Well, Tae Seong called earlier
saying he'd be late,

256
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:01,541
so I washed Yul and put her to bed
in the master bedroom.

257
00:17:01,541 --> 00:17:03,617
Sorry I'm late. Thank you.

258
00:17:03,617 --> 00:17:05,408
Go ahead and do what you need to do.

259
00:17:12,492 --> 00:17:13,503
[My Santa]
<i>Something came up.</i>

260
00:17:13,503 --> 00:17:17,408
<i>I'll be really late tonight.
Don't wait up. Go to bed first.</i>

261
00:17:40,577 --> 00:17:41,726
[Did Kingfisher...]

262
00:17:42,504 --> 00:17:44,275
<i>Did Kingfisher...</i>

263
00:17:45,332 --> 00:17:47,108
<i>see me too?</i>

264
00:18:00,676 --> 00:18:03,208
<i>That man that day...</i>

265
00:18:04,068 --> 00:18:06,688
<i>Was he really Kingfisher?</i>

266
00:18:06,688 --> 00:18:09,241
<i>Goodnight, Tae Seong.</i>

267
00:18:14,744 --> 00:18:16,652
<i>Tae Seong.</i>

268
00:18:16,652 --> 00:18:20,440
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

269
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:22,241
<i>You're a reporter, right?</i>

270
00:18:24,076 --> 00:18:25,021
[Did Kingfisher see me too?]

271
00:18:25,045 --> 00:18:26,443
[That man that day...
Was he really Kingfisher?]

272
00:18:32,384 --> 00:18:35,376
<i>Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene.</i>

273
00:18:35,376 --> 00:18:37,508
<i>A supermarket murder convict died</i>

274
00:18:37,508 --> 00:18:40,988
<i>after being shot while fleeing
an attempted murder.</i>

275
00:18:40,988 --> 00:18:43,983
<i>Jang Eun Hak, previously imprisoned
for the murder of a supermarket couple</i>

276
00:18:43,983 --> 00:18:46,068
<i>in Gangmyeon-dong 20 years ago,</i>

277
00:18:46,068 --> 00:18:50,508
<i>died after attempting another murder
just one month after his release on parole.</i>

278
00:18:52,468 --> 00:18:53,965
[Unusual Alleyway Attack]
<i>Another Kingfisher incident</i>

279
00:18:53,965 --> 00:18:55,772
[Kingfisher Strikes Again Last Night]
<i>occurred last night.</i>

280
00:18:55,772 --> 00:18:57,439
<i>The victim this time was Mr. Jang,</i>

281
00:18:57,439 --> 00:19:00,636
<i>who had brutally murdered
a supermarket-owning couple 20 years ago.</i>

282
00:19:00,636 --> 00:19:02,697
[Supermarket Murder Convict Shot Dead]
<i>He was sentenced to 16 years,</i>

283
00:19:02,697 --> 00:19:04,813
[While Fleeing After Attempted Murder]
<i>and died a month after being paroled,</i>

284
00:19:04,813 --> 00:19:06,204
[Supermarket Couple Murder Found Dead]
<i>a year before his full term,</i>

285
00:19:06,204 --> 00:19:07,604
[One Month After Parole]
<i>sending shock through the community.</i>

286
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:08,604
- <i>Moreover, this incident differs from</i>
- They say Kingfisher

287
00:19:08,604 --> 00:19:09,604
- <i>the previous ones,</i>
- struck again yesterday.

288
00:19:09,604 --> 00:19:10,604
- <i>which mainly occurred</i>
- Really?

289
00:19:10,604 --> 00:19:11,604
- <i>in enclosed, isolated spaces.</i>
- Kingfisher is awesome.

290
00:19:11,604 --> 00:19:13,788
<i>Unlike other Kingfisher cases,</i>

291
00:19:13,788 --> 00:19:17,241
<i>this one occurred in a residential alley,
making it highly unusual.</i>

292
00:19:17,241 --> 00:19:20,175
[Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene]
<i>Shockingly, Mr. Jang was revealed</i>

293
00:19:20,175 --> 00:19:22,541
<i>to have attempted to murder his employer.</i>

294
00:19:22,541 --> 00:19:25,985
<i>Just one month after being paroled,
he had committed another attempted murder,</i>

295
00:19:25,985 --> 00:19:27,388
<i>this time as a flagrant offender.</i>

296
00:19:27,388 --> 00:19:30,496
<i>Furthermore, given the urgent situation
with the suspect on the run,</i>

297
00:19:30,496 --> 00:19:32,508
<i>it is speculated that Kingfisher
may have broken from his usual pattern</i>

298
00:19:32,508 --> 00:19:36,775
<i>and carried out the shooting
in a public place.</i>

299
00:19:37,876 --> 00:19:39,744
Mommy, where is Daddy?

300
00:19:39,744 --> 00:19:41,792
Why isn't Daddy waking up?

301
00:19:41,792 --> 00:19:45,132
Dad? Let Daddy sleep a little longer.

302
00:19:45,132 --> 00:19:47,441
Is Daddy a sleepyhead?

303
00:19:49,052 --> 00:19:51,808
Daddy worked late last night, so he's tired.

304
00:19:51,808 --> 00:19:53,440
What work?

305
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:55,900
Writing articles?

306
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:58,196
What is an article?

307
00:19:58,196 --> 00:20:01,836
An article is something
that tells people in the world

308
00:20:01,836 --> 00:20:07,576
what happened, why it happened,
and what to do now. That's what it does.

309
00:20:07,576 --> 00:20:09,240
Yul, you finished all of this, right?

310
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:12,928
Oh? You did? Then let's have this.

311
00:20:12,928 --> 00:20:15,312
You said you want to be tall
like Mommy and Daddy, right?

312
00:20:15,312 --> 00:20:17,341
Then you need to eat this
and grow big and tall.

313
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:19,208
Here, eat.

314
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,820
Is it good?

315
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:22,868
It is good!

316
00:20:22,868 --> 00:20:24,568
Yeah?

317
00:20:26,616 --> 00:20:27,808
Daddy!

318
00:20:27,808 --> 00:20:30,032
My little precious! Oh, my!

319
00:20:30,032 --> 00:20:32,252
My treasure!

320
00:20:32,252 --> 00:20:34,060
Did you sleep well?

321
00:20:34,060 --> 00:20:35,375
You're already all dressed?

322
00:20:35,375 --> 00:20:39,075
Yeah. I'm dressed, and I ate this too.

323
00:20:39,075 --> 00:20:41,796
I'm going to be this tall, just like you.

324
00:20:41,796 --> 00:20:43,640
Wow, really? Good job.

325
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:44,724
Sorry, I overslept.

326
00:20:44,724 --> 00:20:48,548
I will make it up to you tomorrow, okay?

327
00:20:48,548 --> 00:20:50,856
Oh, my.

328
00:20:50,856 --> 00:20:52,960
Why don't you sleep a little longer?
You're already up?

329
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,908
I have to get to work.

330
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,520
You must have been tired
from working late last night too,

331
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:03,741
and you were probably super busy
all alone today.

332
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:13,528
What? What's with that meaningful look
so early in the morning...

333
00:21:13,528 --> 00:21:14,528
No, it's not that.

334
00:21:14,528 --> 00:21:17,008
It's the look of someone gazing
at someone precious.

335
00:21:19,872 --> 00:21:23,148
Go wash up. I'll make you some toast.

336
00:21:23,148 --> 00:21:24,964
Just a second.

337
00:21:24,964 --> 00:21:27,308
Let me recharge first.

338
00:21:28,332 --> 00:21:30,032
Me too.

339
00:21:33,984 --> 00:21:35,708
Go wash up.

340
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:39,208
I'm having two pieces of toast.

341
00:21:41,208 --> 00:21:43,647
[Resignation Letter]

342
00:21:45,376 --> 00:21:47,116
Are you threatening me now?

343
00:21:47,116 --> 00:21:49,788
Say it to my face.
Don't do this with a piece of paper.

344
00:21:49,788 --> 00:21:51,314
I know there's
a Kingfisher countermeasure meeting today,

345
00:21:51,314 --> 00:21:53,488
chaired by the Commissioner General.

346
00:21:53,488 --> 00:21:54,712
So what?

347
00:21:54,712 --> 00:21:56,112
How many times have chiefs had meetings?

348
00:21:56,112 --> 00:21:57,564
Don't you know
those meetings are just for show?

349
00:21:57,564 --> 00:21:59,272
Then please make sure
this one isn't just for show.

350
00:21:59,272 --> 00:22:00,788
How exactly am I supposed to do that?

351
00:22:00,788 --> 00:22:03,148
What, you want me to put you in charge?

352
00:22:03,148 --> 00:22:04,212
Why would I?

353
00:22:04,212 --> 00:22:06,041
This is my case.

354
00:22:06,768 --> 00:22:09,804
What were you doing yesterday,
and now you come here?

355
00:22:09,804 --> 00:22:12,712
You finally came face-to-face
with the man you wanted to catch so badly.

356
00:22:12,712 --> 00:22:14,641
But why didn't you catch him?

357
00:22:15,544 --> 00:22:17,244
Jeez.

358
00:22:18,124 --> 00:22:21,112
Other stations asked me
whether you deliberately let him get away.

359
00:22:21,112 --> 00:22:24,440
They think you were stalling to give the guy

360
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:26,875
who took your revenge for you time to escape.

361
00:22:28,376 --> 00:22:30,472
If that's the case,

362
00:22:30,472 --> 00:22:33,152
it'll be grounds for an investigation
and disciplinary action.

363
00:22:33,152 --> 00:22:39,402
Including why you were lurking around
Jang Eun Hak at that time.

364
00:22:40,244 --> 00:22:42,841
You don't think this will come up
in today's meeting?

365
00:22:46,836 --> 00:22:50,260
Only you know the truth.

366
00:22:50,260 --> 00:22:51,500
I won't ask you about it.

367
00:22:51,500 --> 00:22:53,375
But you need to let it go too.

368
00:22:54,396 --> 00:22:59,472
If an investigation or disciplinary action
comes up, I'll cover for you.

369
00:22:59,472 --> 00:23:01,172
You can go now.

370
00:23:02,520 --> 00:23:05,192
I won't make excuses.
I'll take responsibility.

371
00:23:05,192 --> 00:23:07,144
If they tell me to accept
the punishment, I will.

372
00:23:07,144 --> 00:23:08,928
If they give me a chance, I'll make it right.

373
00:23:08,928 --> 00:23:10,941
And if neither is possible...

374
00:23:11,238 --> 00:23:12,094
[Resignation Letter]

375
00:23:12,904 --> 00:23:15,120
Please accept my resignation.

376
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:16,896
Hey, take this back.

377
00:23:16,896 --> 00:23:18,356
Hey, Lee Dong Jin.

378
00:23:18,356 --> 00:23:20,108
Hey, Dong Jin.

379
00:23:20,904 --> 00:23:24,341
Jeez, he's bowing, which he never does.

380
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:32,364
Oh, Mr. Lee.

381
00:23:32,364 --> 00:23:35,000
As expected, all the CCTV footage
around the area was wiped.

382
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,640
It was a no-parking zone, so there wasn't
anything useful from dashcams either.

383
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:40,172
There's a public parking lot in the back.

384
00:23:40,172 --> 00:23:41,172
I saw it.

385
00:23:41,172 --> 00:23:42,344
You did?

386
00:23:42,344 --> 00:23:45,168
Most of the people living there
work in the furniture district,

387
00:23:45,168 --> 00:23:48,108
so it's normally deserted at that hour
because everyone goes to bed early.

388
00:23:48,108 --> 00:23:51,041
Jeez, and no word on any witnesses, either.

389
00:23:51,892 --> 00:23:53,244
What about forensics?

390
00:23:53,244 --> 00:23:56,224
Nothing yet. Doesn't look like
they recovered much from the scene.

391
00:23:56,224 --> 00:23:58,892
But you never know what might turn up,
so keep checking regularly.

392
00:23:58,892 --> 00:24:00,424
Okay.

393
00:24:00,424 --> 00:24:02,332
But are you okay, Mr. Lee?

394
00:24:02,332 --> 00:24:05,064
How do you think I feel after letting him
slip away right in front of me?

395
00:24:05,064 --> 00:24:06,468
No, I didn't mean that.

396
00:24:06,468 --> 00:24:09,408
The victim, Jang Eun Hak, is that person...

397
00:24:10,968 --> 00:24:13,036
Enough.

398
00:24:13,036 --> 00:24:16,264
What happened with those couple of
assault suspects from last time?

399
00:24:16,264 --> 00:24:18,240
Nothing yet on that one.

400
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:20,475
The cybercrime unit
hasn't found anything either.

401
00:24:21,904 --> 00:24:24,648
So what are you going to do without me?

402
00:24:24,648 --> 00:24:27,068
What? Why would you be gone?

403
00:24:27,068 --> 00:24:28,768
Where are you going?

404
00:24:30,678 --> 00:24:31,507
[Civil Servant ID, Lee Dong Jin]

405
00:24:32,084 --> 00:24:33,676
You're getting a new mentor soon.

406
00:24:33,676 --> 00:24:38,041
Keep your eyes open
and learn everything you can.

407
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:41,941
And don't make your previous mentor look bad.

408
00:24:45,948 --> 00:24:48,636
Wait, you're not quitting, are you?
You're not, right?

409
00:24:48,636 --> 00:24:50,592
Jeez, where are you going?

410
00:24:50,592 --> 00:24:52,436
I'm going to sleep.

411
00:24:52,436 --> 00:24:53,975
Now of all times?

412
00:24:53,975 --> 00:24:56,214
[Investigative Reporting Team]

413
00:24:56,238 --> 00:24:57,241
[Kwon Tae Seong]

414
00:24:57,241 --> 00:24:58,908
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

415
00:24:58,932 --> 00:24:59,836
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?]

416
00:25:01,741 --> 00:25:02,741
An avenger of justice...

417
00:25:02,741 --> 00:25:04,522
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong
tracked the cases involving Kingfisher]

418
00:25:04,522 --> 00:25:05,298
[and found what they had in common]

419
00:25:07,531 --> 00:25:08,917
[Five Reflections on Kingfisher]

420
00:25:08,942 --> 00:25:11,877
[The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask]

421
00:25:13,341 --> 00:25:15,675
[Even if Kingfisher is caught tomorrow,
the questions he raised will remain]

422
00:25:15,699 --> 00:25:16,647
[Kwon Tae Seong, Social Affairs Reporter]

423
00:25:18,075 --> 00:25:20,360
Wow! As expected of Kwon Tae Seong.

424
00:25:20,360 --> 00:25:23,884
His comeback piece on Kingfisher
is an on-the-ground exclusive too.

425
00:25:23,884 --> 00:25:26,264
Ms. Gu, did you go there with him?

426
00:25:26,264 --> 00:25:29,356
Oh, no, I didn't know about it.

427
00:25:29,356 --> 00:25:32,480
Really? What? He acted like
he wasn't interested,

428
00:25:32,480 --> 00:25:34,852
but he was digging into it on his own?

429
00:25:34,852 --> 00:25:36,768
So it was all an act.

430
00:25:36,768 --> 00:25:37,836
But why isn't he here?

431
00:25:37,836 --> 00:25:40,008
We need a follow-up article fast.

432
00:25:43,308 --> 00:25:46,028
<i>Let's focus on the parole system
for our next piece.</i>

433
00:25:46,028 --> 00:25:50,100
<i>Let's look into possible loopholes
in Jang Eun Hak's parole review process,</i>

434
00:25:50,100 --> 00:25:53,544
<i>and focus on preventive measures
so this kind of thing doesn't happen again.</i>

435
00:25:53,544 --> 00:25:56,296
<i>Based on your research,
prepare a draft article.</i>

436
00:25:56,296 --> 00:25:57,541
<i>I have somewhere else I need to go today.</i>

437
00:25:57,541 --> 00:25:58,672
What's he saying? Why isn't he coming?

438
00:25:58,672 --> 00:26:01,492
Oh, I don't know about that.

439
00:26:01,492 --> 00:26:03,432
He just told me to prepare the article.

440
00:26:03,432 --> 00:26:06,768
Oh! A quick follow-up story? I like it.

441
00:26:06,768 --> 00:26:08,468
What's the angle?

442
00:26:10,316 --> 00:26:14,140
The homework Kingfisher left us?

443
00:26:14,140 --> 00:26:16,996
Oh, homework?

444
00:26:16,996 --> 00:26:18,696
What's that supposed to mean?

445
00:26:25,996 --> 00:26:27,696
Director Yoo

446
00:26:28,308 --> 00:26:32,036
must have been quite surprised
by her husband's article.

447
00:26:32,036 --> 00:26:33,808
She knew about it.

448
00:26:34,732 --> 00:26:38,440
- What?
- She fired, knowing her husband was coming.

449
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:44,316
She probably figured that if she missed
the shot, more people might get hurt.

450
00:26:44,316 --> 00:26:48,156
What if she bumped into her husband?

451
00:26:48,156 --> 00:26:50,508
She probably factored all of that
into her decision.

452
00:26:51,408 --> 00:26:54,175
Because she has never once been wrong.

453
00:26:55,180 --> 00:26:58,768
She's never been wrong. Never made a mistake.

454
00:26:58,768 --> 00:27:02,540
Anyway, Assistant Manager Ki,
you must've had a hard time.

455
00:27:02,540 --> 00:27:07,404
I erased what I could
and checked for witnesses and vehicles,

456
00:27:07,404 --> 00:27:11,816
but the area was huge,
so I'm not sure we covered every route.

457
00:27:11,816 --> 00:27:15,068
We didn't get a chance to check
the new sniper position afterward, either.

458
00:27:15,068 --> 00:27:17,660
Getting out quickly was our priority.

459
00:27:17,660 --> 00:27:20,012
So now,

460
00:27:20,012 --> 00:27:23,052
we don't know where something
could come from, huh?

461
00:27:23,052 --> 00:27:26,968
So far, nothing concerning
has appeared in the police database.

462
00:27:26,968 --> 00:27:29,508
Keep monitoring it closely.

463
00:27:30,252 --> 00:27:34,028
And for the time being,
let's leave out the sniper stuff.

464
00:27:34,028 --> 00:27:35,788
Understood.

465
00:27:35,788 --> 00:27:37,488
Good work.

466
00:27:43,688 --> 00:27:45,940
Let's give you a bath, Tae Soon.

467
00:27:45,940 --> 00:27:49,664
You'll start to smell
if you don't get washed regularly.

468
00:27:49,664 --> 00:27:54,584
Yoo Bo Na must have had a great time,
like flying high, right?

469
00:27:54,584 --> 00:27:56,475
Shall we wash your hair too?

470
00:28:00,948 --> 00:28:05,164
Ah, you're so pretty.

471
00:28:05,164 --> 00:28:08,341
Nice and cool.

472
00:28:27,316 --> 00:28:29,108
Wow, look at all this dust.

473
00:28:30,792 --> 00:28:34,336
How can this be where our Director Yoo stays,
even for a minute?

474
00:28:34,336 --> 00:28:37,432
Jeez, move over there a bit!

475
00:28:37,432 --> 00:28:40,020
I'm going to get lung inflammation
from this, seriously.

476
00:28:40,020 --> 00:28:44,708
I can't sleep at night. I can't sleep.

477
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:49,856
Our great Kingfisher
should be resting well today.

478
00:28:49,856 --> 00:28:52,780
But what is she doing?
Is she sleeping soundly?

479
00:28:52,780 --> 00:28:56,676
Even the way she sleeps must be totally cool.

480
00:28:56,676 --> 00:28:58,572
Oh, seriously, what are these?

481
00:28:58,572 --> 00:29:01,544
Keep this stuff cleaned up!

482
00:29:01,544 --> 00:29:03,541
Jeez.

483
00:29:03,541 --> 00:29:05,420
Ugh. What got on it, seriously?

484
00:29:05,420 --> 00:29:08,041
This is expensive,
and it can't even be dry-cleaned.

485
00:29:09,184 --> 00:29:11,676
How long has that trash been sitting here?

486
00:29:11,676 --> 00:29:14,508
Tae Soon, you got scared, didn't you?

487
00:29:16,241 --> 00:29:18,328
Are you really not going to help?

488
00:29:18,328 --> 00:29:20,028
Clean this up, now!

489
00:29:33,852 --> 00:29:36,180
Training's pretty intense today?

490
00:29:36,180 --> 00:29:38,908
You usually train like this
when you have a lot on your mind.

491
00:29:42,356 --> 00:29:45,172
I felt like my body was a bit stiff.

492
00:29:45,172 --> 00:29:48,741
Yesterday's mission was intense too.
You should get some rest.

493
00:29:52,900 --> 00:29:54,464
What about the shop?

494
00:29:54,464 --> 00:29:56,020
What if a customer comes?

495
00:29:56,020 --> 00:29:59,036
The only customers I have are flies.

496
00:29:59,036 --> 00:30:01,541
Guess I'll help you make a few more sales.

497
00:30:03,788 --> 00:30:06,808
Looks like your husband was at the scene.

498
00:30:08,372 --> 00:30:10,284
It's nothing you need to worry about.

499
00:30:10,284 --> 00:30:12,875
If it's work,
there's no reason for me to worry.

500
00:30:21,684 --> 00:30:24,120
Yul must have grown a lot lately.

501
00:30:24,120 --> 00:30:28,075
She's asking what her daddy does.

502
00:30:29,708 --> 00:30:35,208
I tell her, "Well, your daddy is someone
who does this kind of work."

503
00:30:37,741 --> 00:30:39,941
She may not understand now,

504
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:42,840
but someday she will, right?

505
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:45,320
What kind of person her daddy is.

506
00:30:45,320 --> 00:30:47,641
She'll be proud of him.

507
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:52,341
That's the kind of work he does.

508
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:55,775
It's when he's doing that work
that he really shines.

509
00:30:58,748 --> 00:31:04,175
He does his job, and I do mine.

510
00:31:05,924 --> 00:31:08,564
As for the unavoidable variables
that come up along the way...

511
00:31:08,564 --> 00:31:14,208
well, I'll manage them
just like I did in the field.

512
00:31:15,480 --> 00:31:17,960
Isn't that what you taught me?

513
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:19,316
I did?

514
00:31:19,316 --> 00:31:23,975
Well, that was so long ago.
I barely remember.

515
00:31:29,784 --> 00:31:31,232
[Hye Ri's Mom]
<i>This is Hye Ri's mom.</i>

516
00:31:31,232 --> 00:31:33,376
<i>You got the call from the daycare, right?</i>

517
00:31:33,376 --> 00:31:36,460
<i>Don't you think we need to talk?</i>

518
00:31:36,460 --> 00:31:39,908
Why? What's the problem this time?

519
00:31:40,125 --> 00:31:42,729
[Yul's Daycare]

520
00:31:43,888 --> 00:31:46,341
Yes, Miss.

521
00:31:46,341 --> 00:31:48,041
Yul?

522
00:31:50,564 --> 00:31:52,508
Oh...

523
00:31:52,508 --> 00:31:54,241
Really?

524
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:16,256
<i>Assistant Manager Ki, this is Kwon Se Ah.</i>

525
00:32:16,256 --> 00:32:18,964
<i>I got your number from Bo Na
and wanted to reach out.</i>

526
00:32:18,964 --> 00:32:22,104
<i>I'd like to return your cleaned clothes.</i>

527
00:32:22,104 --> 00:32:25,940
<i>When would be convenient?</i>

528
00:32:29,056 --> 00:32:30,873
<i>Just throw them...</i>

529
00:32:44,964 --> 00:32:46,973
<i>Let's meet after work today.</i>

530
00:32:48,932 --> 00:32:50,812
Today!

531
00:32:50,812 --> 00:32:52,540
Yeah!

532
00:32:52,540 --> 00:32:55,544
Hey, Kwon Se Ah! You can do this, right?

533
00:32:55,544 --> 00:32:56,707
Today's the day!

534
00:32:56,707 --> 00:33:00,207
He said let's meet today,
not tomorrow. What do I do?

535
00:33:00,976 --> 00:33:02,107
Oh?

536
00:33:02,107 --> 00:33:03,907
Oh, jeez.

537
00:33:05,724 --> 00:33:07,060
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>What are you doing now?</i>

538
00:33:07,060 --> 00:33:09,284
<i>I'm a little down today.
Let's just grab a meal.</i>

539
00:33:09,284 --> 00:33:10,984
What?

540
00:33:15,436 --> 00:33:17,552
<i>The customer's phone is turned off...</i>

541
00:33:17,552 --> 00:33:22,407
Seriously, where is he hiding
with his phone turned off?

542
00:33:23,073 --> 00:33:26,332
Was the shock of missing
Kingfisher too much for him?

543
00:33:26,332 --> 00:33:27,907
He's not really quitting, is he?

544
00:33:28,262 --> 00:33:30,071
[You have a new message]

545
00:33:32,273 --> 00:33:34,473
<i>Eat by yourself. I'm busy.</i>

546
00:33:36,020 --> 00:33:39,096
<i>Another date today?
With your sister-in-law again?</i>

547
00:33:39,096 --> 00:33:40,632
<i>No. Today it's with a guy.</i>

548
00:33:40,632 --> 00:33:42,044
Oh, with a guy.

549
00:33:42,044 --> 00:33:44,728
W-W-With a guy?

550
00:33:44,728 --> 00:33:46,428
With who?

551
00:33:52,240 --> 00:33:56,173
Yul, did something happen at kindergarten?

552
00:33:56,988 --> 00:33:58,688
Look at Mommy.

553
00:34:03,760 --> 00:34:06,988
Can you tell me what happened?

554
00:34:06,988 --> 00:34:09,800
That way, I can help you.

555
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:13,964
Yul, I'm your best friend, remember?

556
00:34:13,964 --> 00:34:17,140
Best friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

557
00:34:18,292 --> 00:34:21,840
Mommy...

558
00:34:22,564 --> 00:34:24,192
Mommy.

559
00:34:24,192 --> 00:34:25,384
Oh, I see.

560
00:34:25,384 --> 00:34:28,144
Were you upset?

561
00:34:28,144 --> 00:34:31,140
Oh, dear. You were upset? Okay.

562
00:34:31,140 --> 00:34:33,673
I'm sorry. I understand.

563
00:34:36,580 --> 00:34:38,573
Mommy.

564
00:35:17,672 --> 00:35:21,473
<i>A punk who shot a dad dead</i>

565
00:35:22,356 --> 00:35:25,352
<i>right in front of his seven-year-old son.</i>

566
00:35:25,352 --> 00:35:30,648
<i>The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.</i>

567
00:35:30,648 --> 00:35:36,128
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

568
00:35:36,128 --> 00:35:40,540
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

569
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,384
What is it? What do you want?

570
00:35:53,384 --> 00:35:57,468
Does an elderly lady
and her grandson live here?

571
00:35:57,468 --> 00:35:59,173
An elderly lady?

572
00:35:59,868 --> 00:36:03,256
Oh, you must mean the people
who lived here before.

573
00:36:03,256 --> 00:36:05,907
I moved in last year.

574
00:36:07,476 --> 00:36:09,373
Okay, I see.

575
00:36:09,373 --> 00:36:11,092
[Ongsan Dream Real Estate]
Oh, that old lady?

576
00:36:11,092 --> 00:36:13,566
- She went to a nursing home last year.
- A nursing home?

577
00:36:13,566 --> 00:36:16,400
She had dementia or something
starting a few years ago.

578
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:19,748
She's probably been a bit
in and out of it mentally for a while.

579
00:36:19,748 --> 00:36:23,628
Then what about the kid...
She had a grandson, didn't she?

580
00:36:23,628 --> 00:36:25,228
Her grandson?

581
00:36:25,228 --> 00:36:28,764
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

582
00:36:28,764 --> 00:36:33,708
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

583
00:36:33,708 --> 00:36:36,040
Do you happen to know where he is now?

584
00:36:36,040 --> 00:36:38,080
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

585
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:39,600
Yeah, that's right.

586
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:43,773
There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.

587
00:36:45,752 --> 00:36:47,496
Here.

588
00:36:47,496 --> 00:36:50,200
Sorry I'm returning these so late,
Assistant Manager Ki.

589
00:36:50,200 --> 00:36:52,707
They've been cleaned for a while,

590
00:36:52,707 --> 00:36:56,460
but I wasn't sure
how to get them back to you.

591
00:36:56,460 --> 00:36:58,160
Okay.

592
00:36:59,296 --> 00:37:00,996
Yeah.

593
00:37:02,852 --> 00:37:04,152
Don't you have anything else to say?

594
00:37:04,152 --> 00:37:05,704
Pardon?

595
00:37:05,704 --> 00:37:09,373
Oh, I guess it's my turn to talk.

596
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:12,607
I believe we had a date planned.

597
00:37:15,112 --> 00:37:18,224
Oh, you remember.

598
00:37:18,224 --> 00:37:21,688
Then shall we start with dinner?

599
00:37:21,688 --> 00:37:23,388
I'm fine without eating.

600
00:37:29,312 --> 00:37:31,292
Hey, what are you doing here?

601
00:37:31,292 --> 00:37:33,896
You! Why are you here?
How did you know I was here?

602
00:37:33,896 --> 00:37:34,907
You told me.

603
00:37:34,907 --> 00:37:35,907
Huh?

604
00:37:35,907 --> 00:37:38,807
"Hey, where are you?" "Me? Yun Cafe."

605
00:37:38,807 --> 00:37:40,308
I've been looking everywhere for you.

606
00:37:40,308 --> 00:37:42,216
Why?

607
00:37:42,216 --> 00:37:45,172
Hello. I'm Beom Seong Hun,
Se Dol's friend here.

608
00:37:45,172 --> 00:37:46,368
I've heard a lot about you.

609
00:37:46,368 --> 00:37:48,473
Hey, what have I even said about him...

610
00:37:48,473 --> 00:37:49,473
No, I didn't.

611
00:37:49,473 --> 00:37:50,888
If it's not rude, may I join you?

612
00:37:50,888 --> 00:37:54,232
No, it is rude. It's very rude.
You're being incredibly rude.

613
00:37:54,232 --> 00:37:58,192
Oh, he might seem a bit clueless,
but he's definitely not a bad guy.

614
00:37:58,192 --> 00:38:01,176
First of all, his job is a cop.

615
00:38:01,176 --> 00:38:03,673
Can't you see this isn't exactly
the place for you right now?

616
00:38:03,673 --> 00:38:06,900
Why don't you leave while I'm asking nicely?

617
00:38:06,900 --> 00:38:09,276
Hey, why isn't this the place for me?

618
00:38:09,276 --> 00:38:10,916
Don't you know the world is
a dangerous place these days?

619
00:38:10,916 --> 00:38:12,229
Even if he looks innocent on the outside,

620
00:38:12,229 --> 00:38:15,574
an expert like me needs to scan him
and see if he's rotten on the inside.

621
00:38:15,574 --> 00:38:17,107
You, seriously...

622
00:38:18,104 --> 00:38:22,028
Not that I'm saying that's what you are,
of course. Don't get me wrong.

623
00:38:22,028 --> 00:38:25,673
We were just about to
go get something to eat.

624
00:38:26,628 --> 00:38:28,968
Shall we get going?

625
00:38:28,968 --> 00:38:30,160
Oh, food!

626
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:31,307
Hey, perfect timing.

627
00:38:31,307 --> 00:38:33,596
I was just getting hungry.

628
00:38:33,596 --> 00:38:36,740
Well, since we've met like this,
why don't we have a meal together?

629
00:38:36,740 --> 00:38:37,920
I know a good place nearby.

630
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:41,636
Assistant Manager Ki, we'll go ahead.
Can you come out in a little while?

631
00:38:41,636 --> 00:38:43,060
Sure.

632
00:38:43,060 --> 00:38:44,773
- Come on out!
- Hey.

633
00:38:47,780 --> 00:38:48,860
Oh, seriously.

634
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:52,088
Hey, put this down.

635
00:38:52,088 --> 00:38:53,968
Hey, do you have a gun on you right now?

636
00:38:53,968 --> 00:38:55,432
Do you think I would? What's with the gun?

637
00:38:55,432 --> 00:38:57,507
So I can blow your head off!

638
00:38:57,507 --> 00:38:59,407
Hey, that hurts!

639
00:39:00,180 --> 00:39:01,232
I came because I was worried about you, okay?

640
00:39:01,232 --> 00:39:03,340
About what?

641
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:05,288
You know I've got good instincts, right?

642
00:39:05,288 --> 00:39:07,800
Oh, you do? You do?

643
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:10,673
There's something off about that guy.

644
00:39:10,673 --> 00:39:12,812
Like he reeks of a brutal crime or something?

645
00:39:12,812 --> 00:39:15,007
He's my sister-in-law's coworker, got it?

646
00:39:16,212 --> 00:39:19,940
Then that whole company sounds suspicious.

647
00:39:19,940 --> 00:39:21,488
Hmm...

648
00:39:21,488 --> 00:39:23,908
If you don't have a gun,
I'll use my bare hands, you punk!

649
00:39:23,908 --> 00:39:25,540
Why did you come here? Aren't you leaving?

650
00:39:25,540 --> 00:39:28,273
Why'd you come here just to piss me off?

651
00:39:28,273 --> 00:39:30,540
- Hey, that's enough.
- Where is it?

652
00:39:31,908 --> 00:39:33,236
That restaurant.

653
00:39:33,236 --> 00:39:34,936
What?

654
00:39:41,740 --> 00:39:45,364
This is the kind of chicken feet place
you can't quit once you've tried it.

655
00:39:45,364 --> 00:39:48,117
Alright, starting with
whole chicken feet, spicy chicken feet,

656
00:39:48,117 --> 00:39:49,516
boneless chicken feet,
and braised chicken feet.

657
00:39:49,516 --> 00:39:51,988
For the record, our usual move
is to start with the soupy ones

658
00:39:51,988 --> 00:39:53,907
and finish with the grilled spicy ones.

659
00:39:53,907 --> 00:39:55,460
Do you like chicken feet?

660
00:39:55,460 --> 00:39:57,807
Sometimes. Very occasionally.

661
00:39:57,807 --> 00:40:00,807
They're also packed with collagen, you know.

662
00:40:04,248 --> 00:40:05,392
Can't you eat them?

663
00:40:05,392 --> 00:40:09,007
No. I'm going to give them
a try starting today.

664
00:40:09,007 --> 00:40:10,807
Then please enjoy.

665
00:40:20,508 --> 00:40:22,208
Cheers!

666
00:40:25,896 --> 00:40:27,596
Cheers!

667
00:40:30,312 --> 00:40:31,448
This is so good.

668
00:40:31,448 --> 00:40:34,573
You said you're a cop. What division?

669
00:40:35,668 --> 00:40:37,673
Criminal Affairs, Violent Crimes.

670
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:40,672
Oh, Violent Crimes.

671
00:40:40,672 --> 00:40:43,740
You must get some interesting cases.

672
00:40:43,740 --> 00:40:45,388
Plenty of horrible ones.

673
00:40:45,388 --> 00:40:47,580
People die, get hurt, get messed up.

674
00:40:47,580 --> 00:40:50,540
What case have you been working on lately?

675
00:40:52,340 --> 00:40:54,552
That's confidential.

676
00:40:54,552 --> 00:40:58,840
You seem really interested in crime, though?

677
00:40:59,884 --> 00:41:02,088
I'm interested in profiling.

678
00:41:02,088 --> 00:41:04,440
I majored in psychology too.

679
00:41:05,473 --> 00:41:07,892
You majored in psychology.

680
00:41:07,892 --> 00:41:09,607
That's impressive.

681
00:41:10,260 --> 00:41:12,507
Then let me give you a scenario.

682
00:41:12,507 --> 00:41:15,073
Want to try profiling it for fun?

683
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:18,276
Sounds fun.

684
00:41:18,276 --> 00:41:20,448
Okay, a man

685
00:41:20,448 --> 00:41:24,040
was shot dead through a gap
in a motel window by a sniper rifle.

686
00:41:24,712 --> 00:41:26,564
Who's the killer?

687
00:41:26,564 --> 00:41:28,688
Are you kidding? The whole country knows.

688
00:41:28,688 --> 00:41:29,824
It happened yesterday too.

689
00:41:29,824 --> 00:41:31,732
Hey, do you think I'd ask about that?

690
00:41:31,732 --> 00:41:35,240
Who do you think Kingfisher really is?

691
00:41:36,248 --> 00:41:37,948
I'm not sure.

692
00:41:39,020 --> 00:41:43,373
The police don't have enough evidence
to make an inference like that.

693
00:41:44,307 --> 00:41:49,224
The whole process is extremely methodical,
and he leaves no evidence behind.

694
00:41:49,224 --> 00:41:52,407
That's why I have a theory.

695
00:41:52,407 --> 00:41:57,140
"Maybe Kingfisher isn't acting alone?"
That kind of.

696
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,432
That's possible.

697
00:42:00,432 --> 00:42:02,840
His methods do seem highly organized.

698
00:42:04,068 --> 00:42:07,607
But you sound pretty certain, though?

699
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:12,407
That he never leaves any evidence.

700
00:42:13,040 --> 00:42:15,373
That's why the police
haven't caught him yet, right?

701
00:42:16,072 --> 00:42:18,560
Ma'am, one more order of
chicken feet in broth, please.

702
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:20,364
Yeah.

703
00:42:20,364 --> 00:42:21,707
Hey!

704
00:42:21,707 --> 00:42:23,828
Did you really eat all that
by yourself already?

705
00:42:23,828 --> 00:42:25,896
Me?

706
00:42:25,896 --> 00:42:27,596
Oh, my.

707
00:42:33,460 --> 00:42:36,173
Wait, you've got something on you.

708
00:42:46,508 --> 00:42:48,816
Thank you.

709
00:42:48,816 --> 00:42:51,273
It's nice to see someone
with such a good appetite.

710
00:42:54,407 --> 00:42:57,640
I usually eat pretty well.

711
00:42:57,640 --> 00:43:00,007
Assistant Manager Ki,
you should eat some too.

712
00:43:00,007 --> 00:43:03,096
Oh, I'm fine. I don't really eat that much.

713
00:43:03,096 --> 00:43:04,220
Oh, right.

714
00:43:04,220 --> 00:43:06,840
You did say you don't eat much, right?

715
00:43:07,720 --> 00:43:09,496
I should get going.

716
00:43:09,496 --> 00:43:10,673
I need to head back to the station.

717
00:43:10,673 --> 00:43:11,948
Yeah? You sure?

718
00:43:11,948 --> 00:43:13,596
Go ahead, bye.

719
00:43:13,596 --> 00:43:15,436
Don't forget to pay on your way out.

720
00:43:15,436 --> 00:43:17,788
Yeah, just stay and have some fun.

721
00:43:17,788 --> 00:43:20,340
Maybe we'll see each other again sometime.

722
00:43:33,616 --> 00:43:37,240
Wow! Looks like Se Dol
finally escaped the single life.

723
00:43:38,804 --> 00:43:42,007
Jeez, but why do I feel like this?

724
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:51,273
Wow, one beer here costs...

725
00:43:51,273 --> 00:43:53,307
Is this some fancy place?

726
00:43:53,956 --> 00:43:56,907
Everyone, let's be prepared.

727
00:43:56,907 --> 00:44:00,373
We need to nip this in the bud.

728
00:44:07,028 --> 00:44:09,372
Both of you are here as well.

729
00:44:09,372 --> 00:44:11,673
Thanks for showing up.

730
00:44:13,608 --> 00:44:16,280
This isn't just about Hye Ri.

731
00:44:16,280 --> 00:44:21,228
Who knows whose child could be next?

732
00:44:21,228 --> 00:44:24,507
I ordered some beer and snacks. Is beer okay?

733
00:44:24,507 --> 00:44:27,312
Oh, absolutely. Beer sounds great.

734
00:44:27,312 --> 00:44:31,520
Well, since we're at a bar,
we might as well have a drink.

735
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:33,584
What are you talking about, beer?

736
00:44:33,584 --> 00:44:36,868
We left the kids at home,
so let's keep this short and wrap it up.

737
00:44:36,868 --> 00:44:41,624
Just because of some stupid blocks,
those two kids ganged up and hurt Hye Ri.

738
00:44:41,624 --> 00:44:44,456
She must've been so upset.

739
00:44:44,456 --> 00:44:47,240
She came home and wouldn't even
eat her favorite pork cutlet...

740
00:44:49,028 --> 00:44:50,564
Oh, my.

741
00:44:50,564 --> 00:44:53,204
What's this?

742
00:44:53,204 --> 00:44:56,007
Is that Yul's finger?

743
00:44:56,916 --> 00:44:59,264
Oh, my God. What happened?

744
00:44:59,264 --> 00:45:01,656
Every time Seo Jun built something
with the blocks,

745
00:45:01,656 --> 00:45:03,172
Hye Ri would come and knock it down.

746
00:45:03,172 --> 00:45:06,607
So Yul tried to stop her.

747
00:45:06,607 --> 00:45:10,840
Then Hye Ri bit Yul's finger.

748
00:45:11,956 --> 00:45:15,976
Seo Jun got scared and pushed Hye Ri away.

749
00:45:15,976 --> 00:45:18,744
As far as he's concerned,
he was only trying to separate them.

750
00:45:18,744 --> 00:45:22,632
Wait, Hye Ri bit Yul?

751
00:45:22,632 --> 00:45:24,260
Hye Ri didn't mention any of that.

752
00:45:24,260 --> 00:45:28,904
Oh, maybe she was afraid you'd scold her,
so she didn't tell you.

753
00:45:28,904 --> 00:45:31,728
Oh, that must've hurt.

754
00:45:31,728 --> 00:45:36,907
Why didn't Yul tell the teacher about this?

755
00:45:38,528 --> 00:45:39,528
Wait.

756
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:43,192
So did you call us here
to complain about this?

757
00:45:43,192 --> 00:45:45,640
To get an apology out of me?

758
00:45:46,676 --> 00:45:48,907
Hye Ri's mom.

759
00:45:48,907 --> 00:45:50,407
Yeah?

760
00:45:50,407 --> 00:45:54,040
No, why? What is it?

761
00:45:55,044 --> 00:46:00,307
As a mom, what am I supposed
to do in a situation like this...

762
00:46:01,580 --> 00:46:03,736
I honestly don't know.

763
00:46:03,736 --> 00:46:07,507
So I just told Yul what felt right to me.

764
00:46:07,507 --> 00:46:09,501
I told Yul that Hye Ri didn't do it
because she hated Yul.

765
00:46:09,501 --> 00:46:12,207
She was probably just upset for a moment.

766
00:46:17,232 --> 00:46:21,360
Well, the kids still have to
live together going forward.

767
00:46:21,360 --> 00:46:23,856
We need to comfort them
so this doesn't leave a bad memory,

768
00:46:23,856 --> 00:46:28,706
and help them get along better from now on.

769
00:46:28,706 --> 00:46:33,173
I think that's what adults should do.

770
00:46:33,792 --> 00:46:39,116
So I wanted to ask for your advice
on how to do that.

771
00:46:39,116 --> 00:46:40,880
Oh, what is there to do?

772
00:46:40,880 --> 00:46:44,040
Just discipline them
if they did something wrong,

773
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:49,136
have them apologize if they need to,
and let the moms clear the air. That's all.

774
00:46:49,136 --> 00:46:50,605
- That's right.
- Yeah.

775
00:46:50,605 --> 00:46:52,536
Right.

776
00:46:52,536 --> 00:46:54,873
Oh, the drinks are here.

777
00:46:58,924 --> 00:47:00,624
Thank you.

778
00:47:01,988 --> 00:47:04,556
Oh, you made it?

779
00:47:04,556 --> 00:47:06,573
Sorry I'm late.

780
00:47:08,336 --> 00:47:10,304
Just a second.

781
00:47:10,304 --> 00:47:13,540
Oh, I saw some blood earlier,
and I'm still feeling queasy.

782
00:47:22,707 --> 00:47:24,592
Hye Ri's mom is...

783
00:47:24,592 --> 00:47:26,332
- Over here.
- Here.

784
00:47:26,332 --> 00:47:28,584
Oh, there you are.

785
00:47:28,584 --> 00:47:32,373
Hye Ri's mom, I heard
our Seo Jun pushed Hye Ri.

786
00:47:32,373 --> 00:47:35,380
That little punk.

787
00:47:35,380 --> 00:47:39,052
I'll give him a good talking-to
when I get home.

788
00:47:39,052 --> 00:47:41,224
I'll make him write an apology letter too.

789
00:47:41,224 --> 00:47:44,340
But I heard he already apologized to Hye Ri.

790
00:47:44,944 --> 00:47:46,496
Yes, he did.

791
00:47:46,496 --> 00:47:49,308
Yes, he apologized.

792
00:47:49,308 --> 00:47:51,140
Well, that's good.

793
00:47:52,716 --> 00:47:54,997
I'll apologize too, on behalf of his mom.

794
00:47:54,997 --> 00:47:57,407
- Well...
- I'm sorry, Hye Ri's mom.

795
00:47:58,436 --> 00:48:00,207
Wow!

796
00:48:00,207 --> 00:48:03,707
That's a bold apology.

797
00:48:09,318 --> 00:48:11,018
I...

798
00:48:13,700 --> 00:48:15,400
Sor...

799
00:48:16,752 --> 00:48:18,444
What should I do?

800
00:48:18,444 --> 00:48:21,473
Do you think Yul will be okay
without going to the hospital?

801
00:48:24,180 --> 00:48:27,764
Oh, it went down pretty quickly
after I put some medicine on it.

802
00:48:27,764 --> 00:48:29,172
Thanks for asking.

803
00:48:29,172 --> 00:48:31,773
- Oh, good.
- What a relief.

804
00:48:32,912 --> 00:48:35,124
Wow, this is great, right?

805
00:48:35,124 --> 00:48:38,780
Let's have a proper drink
and loosen up. Cheers.

806
00:48:38,780 --> 00:48:40,524
- Out of drinks.
- Oh, no beer.

807
00:48:40,524 --> 00:48:41,896
Can I have a glass of beer?

808
00:48:41,896 --> 00:48:44,773
- Here, you can have some of mine for now.
- Okay, sure.

809
00:48:47,800 --> 00:48:49,408
Cheers.

810
00:48:49,408 --> 00:48:51,740
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

811
00:48:59,619 --> 00:49:01,000
Well...

812
00:49:01,000 --> 00:49:05,576
Assistant Manager Ki,
did I happen to do something wrong?

813
00:49:05,576 --> 00:49:07,276
Not at all.

814
00:49:08,132 --> 00:49:12,556
You just seem pretty different from
how you were at the restaurant.

815
00:49:12,556 --> 00:49:14,960
You haven't said much at all.

816
00:49:14,960 --> 00:49:17,628
This is the real me.
Earlier, I was putting on an act.

817
00:49:17,628 --> 00:49:20,200
Why would you do that?

818
00:49:20,200 --> 00:49:21,260
Do you like me?

819
00:49:21,260 --> 00:49:23,216
Yeah, I mean, no.

820
00:49:27,964 --> 00:49:29,300
Yeah.

821
00:49:29,300 --> 00:49:32,128
I'm sorry, but I have no interest in you.

822
00:49:32,128 --> 00:49:33,983
You're not my type.

823
00:49:34,812 --> 00:49:36,888
I'm sorry for asking you out.

824
00:49:36,888 --> 00:49:38,888
It was way too impulsive.

825
00:49:38,888 --> 00:49:40,776
Sorry.

826
00:49:40,776 --> 00:49:43,516
That's what I wanted to tell you,
so I asked to see you today.

827
00:49:46,684 --> 00:49:50,824
Then what is your type?

828
00:49:50,824 --> 00:49:52,524
I'm...

829
00:49:55,236 --> 00:49:58,316
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

830
00:49:58,316 --> 00:50:00,032
Eat up and relax, rookie.

831
00:50:00,032 --> 00:50:02,440
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

832
00:50:02,440 --> 00:50:04,316
but chooses not to.

833
00:50:06,549 --> 00:50:09,849
That's quite a unique preference.

834
00:50:13,004 --> 00:50:16,788
But Assistant Manager Ki,
you don't even know me.

835
00:50:16,788 --> 00:50:18,760
That's right.

836
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:21,083
And I don't particularly want to know you.

837
00:50:26,216 --> 00:50:27,848
Okay!

838
00:50:27,848 --> 00:50:30,649
Found today's punching bag.

839
00:50:30,649 --> 00:50:32,649
- Found one.
- Found one.

840
00:50:39,335 --> 00:50:40,702
[Cybercrime Unit, Sergeant Kim]

841
00:50:44,324 --> 00:50:46,588
- Yes, Mr. Kim.
- Hey, Mr. Beom. It's me.

842
00:50:46,588 --> 00:50:48,232
Guess what I found?

843
00:50:48,232 --> 00:50:49,649
I sent you a link.
Can you check it right away?

844
00:50:49,649 --> 00:50:52,349
Sure. Give me a second.

845
00:50:57,340 --> 00:50:59,583
<i>Hello, gentlemen!</i>

846
00:50:59,583 --> 00:51:02,283
- <i>It's time for Mace Man's justice.</i>
- <i>Justice!</i>

847
00:51:02,283 --> 00:51:05,264
<i>Let's get things started with a bang.</i>

848
00:51:05,264 --> 00:51:06,264
What's this?

849
00:51:06,264 --> 00:51:08,649
Apparently, it's a streaming site
that's been growing underground lately.

850
00:51:08,649 --> 00:51:11,412
They livestream violent or obscene videos,

851
00:51:11,412 --> 00:51:12,856
and apparently get paid in
some kind of cryptocurrency.

852
00:51:12,856 --> 00:51:17,436
<i>Who are we going to teach a lesson today?</i>

853
00:51:17,436 --> 00:51:19,016
<i>Let's go with a pretty one, if possible.</i>

854
00:51:19,016 --> 00:51:21,256
<i>You won't be able to see their faces
once they're covered in blood, idiot.</i>

855
00:51:21,256 --> 00:51:23,288
See them? Three masked men.

856
00:51:23,288 --> 00:51:26,436
These guys look like the couple-assault
suspects you've been after, right?

857
00:51:26,436 --> 00:51:29,016
Oh, you're right.

858
00:51:29,016 --> 00:51:32,132
Man, so cryptocurrency was their motive?

859
00:51:32,132 --> 00:51:33,340
Does it show where they are?

860
00:51:33,340 --> 00:51:34,624
It says Songju Park.

861
00:51:34,624 --> 00:51:35,920
Songju Park?

862
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:37,449
Huh? That's nearby.

863
00:51:37,449 --> 00:51:40,744
<i>So what do you think of
these punks, gentlemen?</i>

864
00:51:40,744 --> 00:51:43,249
<i>Zoom in on the woman's face.</i>

865
00:51:43,249 --> 00:51:45,772
<i>Let's see.</i>

866
00:51:45,772 --> 00:51:47,984
- Huh?
- <i>There.</i>

867
00:51:47,984 --> 00:51:49,140
Darn it.

868
00:51:49,140 --> 00:51:50,840
Ah, well...

869
00:51:51,704 --> 00:51:54,396
Mr. Kim, please call for backup
from the local precinct,

870
00:51:54,396 --> 00:51:55,883
and send ambulances to Songju Park.

871
00:51:55,883 --> 00:51:57,352
- Three ambulances.
- Three?

872
00:51:57,352 --> 00:52:00,948
- Not two?
- No, three. Make sure it's three.

873
00:52:00,948 --> 00:52:04,104
No. Kwon Se Ah, please!

874
00:52:04,104 --> 00:52:05,804
This way, right?

875
00:52:06,424 --> 00:52:08,132
What are they doing?

876
00:52:08,132 --> 00:52:09,692
Why are they just walking?

877
00:52:09,692 --> 00:52:12,404
The guy's obviously a pathetic loser.

878
00:52:12,404 --> 00:52:14,872
He can't even hold her hand.

879
00:52:14,872 --> 00:52:20,749
Well, gentlemen,
I think it's time to teach them a lesson.

880
00:52:23,012 --> 00:52:24,477
I've already been rejected,

881
00:52:24,477 --> 00:52:27,349
but since I started this confession anyway,
let me just finish it.

882
00:52:28,644 --> 00:52:33,624
The first day we met,
when you said you'd help me find Yul,

883
00:52:33,624 --> 00:52:38,152
that's when you dove straight into my heart.

884
00:52:38,152 --> 00:52:39,852
And...

885
00:52:42,220 --> 00:52:43,920
Who on earth are you?

886
00:52:45,244 --> 00:52:46,944
Wait...

887
00:52:49,288 --> 00:52:51,716
Assistant Manager Ki, are you okay?

888
00:52:54,096 --> 00:52:55,916
<i>I'm...</i>

889
00:52:55,916 --> 00:52:59,276
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

890
00:52:59,276 --> 00:53:02,300
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

891
00:53:02,300 --> 00:53:03,483
<i>but chooses not to.</i>

892
00:53:03,483 --> 00:53:06,169
[Kwon Se Ah, Current: Graduate student,
College of Physical Education]

893
00:53:06,169 --> 00:53:07,150
[Former: Women's Judo National Team Reserve]

894
00:53:08,060 --> 00:53:09,388
Kwon Se Ah, please.

895
00:53:09,388 --> 00:53:12,849
Take it easy. Don't kill them.

896
00:53:15,732 --> 00:53:17,483
Assistant Manager Ki!

897
00:53:17,483 --> 00:53:21,292
Yeah, I'm... I'm fine.

898
00:53:21,292 --> 00:53:22,716
Oh, no, what do I do?

899
00:53:22,716 --> 00:53:25,416
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

900
00:53:25,416 --> 00:53:26,988
Oh, dear.

901
00:53:26,988 --> 00:53:29,132
Oh, please don't come any closer.

902
00:53:29,132 --> 00:53:32,216
Please, just stay back.

903
00:53:34,929 --> 00:53:38,149
Oh, my tailbone... Oh...

904
00:53:38,149 --> 00:53:41,000
Jeez, I said stay back.

905
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:43,483
Oh, my, are you okay?

906
00:53:43,483 --> 00:53:45,076
Oh...

907
00:53:45,076 --> 00:53:47,349
Stay still! Don't move!

908
00:53:47,349 --> 00:53:49,220
Darn, this is so embarrassing.

909
00:53:49,220 --> 00:53:51,212
Hey, take out that punk first!

910
00:53:51,212 --> 00:53:53,949
If you keep doing this,
I'm seriously going to call the police...

911
00:54:02,096 --> 00:54:04,516
No time for that.

912
00:54:06,520 --> 00:54:08,828
Oh, I'm terrified.

913
00:54:08,828 --> 00:54:12,149
Assistant Manager Ki,
that must've scared you, right?

914
00:54:15,549 --> 00:54:18,083
It... did.

915
00:54:19,188 --> 00:54:20,536
They just came out of nowhere.

916
00:54:20,536 --> 00:54:21,816
Hey, Kwon Se Ah!

917
00:54:21,816 --> 00:54:22,816
Huh? What?

918
00:54:22,816 --> 00:54:24,076
Hey, you!

919
00:54:24,076 --> 00:54:26,096
You...

920
00:54:26,096 --> 00:54:27,724
I knew you'd pull something like this.

921
00:54:27,724 --> 00:54:29,296
Huh?

922
00:54:29,296 --> 00:54:30,920
Hey!

923
00:54:30,920 --> 00:54:33,696
Hey, look at what you've done to him...

924
00:54:33,696 --> 00:54:36,479
I told you not to use
your techniques carelessly, right?

925
00:54:36,479 --> 00:54:39,540
Well... It just happened automatically.

926
00:54:39,540 --> 00:54:41,896
Hey, wake up!

927
00:54:41,896 --> 00:54:45,040
Are you okay? Hey!

928
00:54:45,040 --> 00:54:48,048
Wow, he passed out cold.

929
00:54:48,048 --> 00:54:50,336
Okay, no visible injuries.

930
00:54:50,336 --> 00:54:52,084
And you're not hurt anywhere, right?
Of course not.

931
00:54:52,084 --> 00:54:54,112
- Yeah.
- And you...

932
00:54:54,112 --> 00:54:56,916
barely had to lift a finger anyway.

933
00:55:06,976 --> 00:55:09,416
Oh, nice timing.

934
00:55:10,940 --> 00:55:12,849
[Beom Seong Hun, Current:
Nambu Station's Youngest Detective]

935
00:55:12,849 --> 00:55:14,446
[Former: Asian Games Gold Medalist
in Men's Judo, Special Police Hire]

936
00:55:14,849 --> 00:55:16,376
Don't move.

937
00:55:16,376 --> 00:55:21,212
You're under arrest for aggravated assault
and obstruction of official duties.

938
00:55:21,212 --> 00:55:25,032
You have the right
to remain silent and to an attorney.

939
00:55:25,032 --> 00:55:27,416
Oh, right. And anything stupid you say
can be used against you,

940
00:55:27,416 --> 00:55:29,416
so watch what you say.

941
00:55:31,049 --> 00:55:34,216
Mr. Tiger! True colors of a cop!
Champions of justice!

942
00:55:34,216 --> 00:55:35,476
- Hey!
- Hey!

943
00:55:35,476 --> 00:55:38,483
- Take them down and finish it!
- Take them down and finish it!

944
00:55:38,483 --> 00:55:39,949
- You remember?
- Hey, how do you know that?

945
00:55:39,949 --> 00:55:42,356
- This is nothing.
- Hey, what's going on here?

946
00:55:42,356 --> 00:55:44,304
- A throw.
- Hey, that's not right!

947
00:55:44,304 --> 00:55:46,108
No, you do it from here, like this!

948
00:55:46,108 --> 00:55:47,349
- Bam!
- Oh!

949
00:55:47,349 --> 00:55:50,492
What was that? Wow, you're good.

950
00:55:50,492 --> 00:55:53,004
- Of course, I'm a cop.
- Jeez.

951
00:55:53,004 --> 00:55:55,449
The police will be here soon...

952
00:55:57,664 --> 00:55:59,364
The kid...

953
00:56:00,064 --> 00:56:02,944
She's getting harder and harder to handle.

954
00:56:02,944 --> 00:56:06,664
Of course. The older they get,
the less they listen.

955
00:56:06,664 --> 00:56:10,312
I complained to my mom once,
and you know what she said?

956
00:56:10,312 --> 00:56:11,740
Did she say she'd scold your kid?

957
00:56:11,740 --> 00:56:14,649
She said my kid's
exactly like I was as a kid.

958
00:56:16,048 --> 00:56:19,483
She prayed for me
to have a daughter just like me,

959
00:56:20,748 --> 00:56:23,324
and her wish came true.

960
00:56:23,324 --> 00:56:25,416
That scared me more than anything.

961
00:56:25,416 --> 00:56:27,560
"A daughter who takes after me."

962
00:56:27,560 --> 00:56:31,064
Kids are half born that way
and half learn by watching.

963
00:56:31,064 --> 00:56:35,876
That's why they say,
"A child is a reflection of their parents."

964
00:56:35,876 --> 00:56:39,072
That saying, that one really hits me hard.

965
00:56:39,072 --> 00:56:41,832
I mean, isn't that a little unfair to me?

966
00:56:41,832 --> 00:56:47,016
All the time and effort I put into her...

967
00:56:48,696 --> 00:56:50,760
Jeez.

968
00:56:50,760 --> 00:56:52,088
Hold on.

969
00:56:52,088 --> 00:56:54,720
- It's your husband.
- Your husband.

970
00:56:54,720 --> 00:56:56,420
What?

971
00:56:57,216 --> 00:56:59,183
What time is it right now?

972
00:56:59,183 --> 00:57:01,624
Look at the clock.

973
00:57:01,624 --> 00:57:04,420
You come home at midnight every day,

974
00:57:04,420 --> 00:57:08,784
and you're complaining about
having to watch the kid one day early?

975
00:57:08,784 --> 00:57:10,216
What, her bath?

976
00:57:10,216 --> 00:57:13,904
Just give her a bath yourself.

977
00:57:13,904 --> 00:57:17,216
I don't know. Just put her to bed.

978
00:57:18,192 --> 00:57:20,116
Or whatever.

979
00:57:20,836 --> 00:57:24,272
Seriously, how is he exactly like my husband?

980
00:57:24,272 --> 00:57:25,716
We had this kid together,

981
00:57:25,716 --> 00:57:30,096
so why am I the one expected to do
all the parenting?

982
00:57:30,096 --> 00:57:31,476
If this is how it's going to be,

983
00:57:31,476 --> 00:57:33,268
he shouldn't have been begging
for a second kid.

984
00:57:33,268 --> 00:57:35,040
Well, my husband,

985
00:57:35,040 --> 00:57:38,412
even when I beg him to play
with the kids instead of drinking,

986
00:57:38,412 --> 00:57:40,856
all he ever says is, "Yeah, yeah."

987
00:57:40,856 --> 00:57:42,649
And one time,

988
00:57:43,580 --> 00:57:45,209
he called saying he was leaving,

989
00:57:45,209 --> 00:57:46,776
and then he took so long to show up
that I went down to check,

990
00:57:46,776 --> 00:57:49,783
and there he was, sleeping
in the parking lot. This guy, seriously.

991
00:57:49,783 --> 00:57:50,783
In the car?

992
00:57:50,783 --> 00:57:52,108
Yeah.

993
00:57:52,108 --> 00:57:53,628
What a gentleman.

994
00:57:53,628 --> 00:57:54,804
What?

995
00:57:54,804 --> 00:57:57,820
I got a call from the security office
once about Hye Ri's dad.

996
00:57:57,820 --> 00:57:59,983
They said he was snoring
away in the elevator.

997
00:57:59,983 --> 00:58:01,016
Oh, God.

998
00:58:01,016 --> 00:58:04,483
What if the kids learn from watching them?

999
00:58:05,488 --> 00:58:08,716
Then just raise them alone as I do.

1000
00:58:15,972 --> 00:58:17,524
What about you, Yul's mom?

1001
00:58:17,524 --> 00:58:19,320
What?

1002
00:58:19,320 --> 00:58:20,932
Yul's dad.

1003
00:58:20,932 --> 00:58:23,040
I'm curious what kind of dad Yul has.

1004
00:58:23,040 --> 00:58:25,949
Yeah, me too. What's he like?

1005
00:58:27,428 --> 00:58:29,449
My husband?

1006
00:58:35,020 --> 00:58:36,668
Did my little girl get hurt a lot?

1007
00:58:36,668 --> 00:58:39,360
Yeah, it hurt a lot.

1008
00:58:39,360 --> 00:58:44,112
It's okay. I put some medicine on it,
so it'll get better soon.

1009
00:58:44,112 --> 00:58:47,749
What made you the saddest today, Yul?

1010
00:58:49,276 --> 00:58:51,116
Hye Ri cried today.

1011
00:58:51,116 --> 00:58:53,736
Oh, did seeing Hye Ri cry
make you the saddest?

1012
00:58:53,736 --> 00:58:56,928
- Yeah.
- Why did that make you so sad?

1013
00:58:56,928 --> 00:59:02,216
Because Mommy told me
to get along with my friends.

1014
00:59:02,216 --> 00:59:07,048
Oh, you wanted to get along
with your friend, but it didn't work out?

1015
00:59:07,048 --> 00:59:10,704
Yeah. But we shouldn't hurt our friends.

1016
00:59:10,704 --> 00:59:12,804
That's right. We shouldn't hurt our friends.

1017
00:59:12,804 --> 00:59:17,004
- No biting and no pushing, right?
- Yeah.

1018
00:59:17,004 --> 00:59:21,354
But sometimes things like that happen
when you're playing with friends.

1019
00:59:21,354 --> 00:59:22,580
What should you do then?

1020
00:59:22,580 --> 00:59:24,192
I should say "Sorry."

1021
00:59:24,192 --> 00:59:25,192
That's right.

1022
00:59:25,192 --> 00:59:29,472
Apologize, make up, and be friends again.

1023
00:59:29,472 --> 00:59:32,188
Yeah, I'll give them presents
and ask them to play with me.

1024
00:59:32,188 --> 00:59:34,932
Wow, your friends are going to love that.

1025
00:59:34,932 --> 00:59:38,580
Then how about we pick out presents
for your friends together tomorrow?

1026
00:59:38,580 --> 00:59:40,016
- Yeah.
- Good.

1027
00:59:40,016 --> 00:59:42,456
Now, what should we play?

1028
00:59:42,456 --> 00:59:43,516
Superman?

1029
00:59:43,516 --> 00:59:45,140
Alright, arms out! Superman!

1030
00:59:45,140 --> 00:59:46,983
Stretch!

1031
00:59:46,983 --> 00:59:48,916
Wow!

1032
00:59:52,584 --> 00:59:55,008
They say the one who throws the punch
sleeps like a baby.

1033
00:59:55,008 --> 00:59:58,683
Even the punk who threatened the chief
seems pretty darn comfortable.

1034
01:00:00,648 --> 01:00:02,783
Hey, Lee Dong Jin, wake up.

1035
01:00:04,196 --> 01:00:06,016
Wake up, now!

1036
01:00:08,696 --> 01:00:11,307
God, because of you,
I made a total fool of myself

1037
01:00:11,307 --> 01:00:13,264
in front of the commissioner today...

1038
01:00:13,264 --> 01:00:16,416
God, why did I ever bring in
a blockhead like you?

1039
01:00:16,416 --> 01:00:18,040
You...

1040
01:00:18,040 --> 01:00:20,252
You have to risk your life.

1041
01:00:20,252 --> 01:00:22,449
Otherwise, we're both going down.

1042
01:00:22,449 --> 01:00:23,464
What?

1043
01:00:23,464 --> 01:00:24,940
What are you doing?

1044
01:00:24,940 --> 01:00:27,349
Move it and pack your stuff, you punk!

1045
01:00:34,549 --> 01:00:37,368
<i>♪ Every day on the bus to school ♪</i>

1046
01:00:37,368 --> 01:00:40,816
<i>♪ I like the girl
who always sits in the same seat ♪</i>

1047
01:00:40,816 --> 01:00:44,236
<i>♪ I sometimes deliberately stand beside her ♪</i>

1048
01:00:44,236 --> 01:00:47,616
<i>♪ But somehow I feel like
I'm not good enough ♪</i>

1049
01:00:47,616 --> 01:00:50,949
<i>♪ No, I'm fine. Don't worry about it ♪</i>

1050
01:00:50,949 --> 01:00:54,383
- <i>♪ I don't have a boyfriend now ♪</i>
- Come on out.

1051
01:00:54,383 --> 01:00:58,700
<i>♪ But why won't you say a word? ♪</i>

1052
01:00:58,700 --> 01:01:01,949
<i>♪ I know you really need me ♪</i>

1053
01:01:01,949 --> 01:01:06,549
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1054
01:01:06,549 --> 01:01:11,292
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1055
01:01:11,292 --> 01:01:16,849
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1056
01:01:22,749 --> 01:01:25,683
<i>♪ Hesitating over something so simple ♪</i>

1057
01:01:25,683 --> 01:01:29,683
<i>♪ Watching you be so hopelessly
hesitant drives me crazy ♪</i>

1058
01:01:29,683 --> 01:01:33,749
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1059
01:01:33,749 --> 01:01:38,920
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1060
01:01:38,920 --> 01:01:44,149
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1061
01:01:52,060 --> 01:01:55,116
I used to be better at this.

1062
01:01:57,449 --> 01:01:58,836
Yul's mom, sing one too.

1063
01:01:58,836 --> 01:02:00,449
- Oh, this is so much fun.
- Sing a song.

1064
01:02:00,449 --> 01:02:01,483
- Come on, sing.
- Me?

1065
01:02:01,483 --> 01:02:02,483
- No, I can't.
- We can't be the only ones singing.

1066
01:02:02,483 --> 01:02:03,483
- A song?
- Sing one!

1067
01:02:03,483 --> 01:02:07,749
- Sing a song!
- Sing a song!

1068
01:02:07,909 --> 01:02:12,616
[A Million Roses]

1069
01:02:16,748 --> 01:02:21,349
<i>♪ Long ago, from some distant star ♪</i>

1070
01:02:22,149 --> 01:02:28,016
<i>♪ When I came into this world ♪</i>

1071
01:02:28,016 --> 01:02:33,900
<i>♪ I heard a small voice ♪</i>

1072
01:02:33,900 --> 01:02:39,692
<i>♪ Telling me to come give love ♪</i>

1073
01:02:39,692 --> 01:02:43,092
<i>♪ That only blooms when you love ♪</i>

1074
01:02:43,092 --> 01:02:45,536
She's surprisingly romantic.

1075
01:02:45,536 --> 01:02:47,449
Exactly.

1076
01:02:47,449 --> 01:02:50,736
Why is she singing such a gloomy song?

1077
01:02:50,736 --> 01:02:53,349
She's killing the mood.

1078
01:02:53,349 --> 01:02:57,284
She's quite something.

1079
01:02:57,284 --> 01:03:03,072
<i>♪ Roses of love in bloom ♪</i>

1080
01:03:03,072 --> 01:03:08,788
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1081
01:03:08,788 --> 01:03:14,748
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1082
01:03:14,748 --> 01:03:20,616
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1083
01:03:20,616 --> 01:03:26,528
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1084
01:03:26,528 --> 01:03:32,380
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1085
01:03:32,380 --> 01:03:37,549
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1086
01:03:38,160 --> 01:03:44,024
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1087
01:03:44,024 --> 01:03:49,083
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1088
01:03:52,836 --> 01:03:55,920
<i>A special task force has been formed</i>

1089
01:03:55,920 --> 01:03:59,100
<i>to apprehend the serial killer
known as Kingfisher.</i>

1090
01:03:59,100 --> 01:04:01,505
<i>Accordingly, the scattered
investigative information and personnel</i>

1091
01:04:01,505 --> 01:04:03,592
<i>from each case
are expected to be consolidated,</i>

1092
01:04:03,592 --> 01:04:08,783
<i>with dedicated staff assigned
to accelerate the Kingfisher investigation.</i>

1093
01:04:39,783 --> 01:04:42,016
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1094
01:04:42,016 --> 01:04:48,916
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1095
01:04:57,816 --> 01:05:01,249
<i>Will this finally end with
Kingfisher's arrest?</i>

1096
01:05:01,249 --> 01:05:06,016
<i>Attention is now focused on
the newly formed Kingfisher task force.</i>

1097
01:06:04,916 --> 01:06:08,936
[A Bona Fide Killer]

1098
01:06:08,960 --> 01:06:11,049
The mugging during the World Cup?

1099
01:06:11,049 --> 01:06:14,549
I believe it could provide a clue
to Kingfisher's identity.

1100
01:06:14,549 --> 01:06:16,420
Do you remember the caller's voice?

1101
01:06:16,420 --> 01:06:18,196
The message on the first card
they sent was...

1102
01:06:18,196 --> 01:06:20,640
"I hope you find your own beautiful scenery."

1103
01:06:20,640 --> 01:06:22,883
Can you tell me anything
about the person sending the flowers?

1104
01:06:22,883 --> 01:06:24,783
Who is it? The person you saw that day.

1105
01:06:24,783 --> 01:06:25,783
Some woman.

1106
01:06:25,783 --> 01:06:27,428
Why are you looking for that woman?

1107
01:06:27,428 --> 01:06:30,236
She either witnessed Kingfisher,
or she is Kingfisher.

1108
01:06:30,236 --> 01:06:32,349
You should still have
the voice message on your phone.

1109
01:06:32,349 --> 01:06:33,349
Who's taking this case?

1110
01:06:33,349 --> 01:06:36,960
We'll set a trap around Gu Jung Yeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

1111
01:06:36,960 --> 01:06:38,583
Client meeting starts.

1112
01:06:38,583 --> 01:06:41,183
Let's go catch Kingfisher.
